<title>JAPAN: Big Japan banks' 1996/97 operating profit forecast.</title>
<headline>Big Japan banks' 1996/97 operating profit forecast.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's ten big commercial banks, or so-called &quot;city banks&quot;, made the following forecasts for parent operating profits for the year ending March 31, 1997 on Friday. (In billions of yen, with actual profits for 1995/96).</p>
<p>				    1996/97	   1995/1996</p>
<p> Dai-Ichi Kangyo    340.0		519.1</p>
<p> Sumitomo	     300.0		414.3</p>
<p> Sanwa		  310.0		490.9</p>
<p> Sakura		 250.0		333.2</p>
<p> BOT-Mitsubishi     440.0		645.0</p>
<p> Fuji		   290.0		466.6</p>
<p> Tokai		  150.0		225.1</p>
<p> Asahi		  140.0		203.4</p>
<p> Daiwa		   80.0		141.6</p>
<p> Hokkaido Takushoku  40.0		 60.8</p>
<p>The full names of the banks are Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank Ltd, Sumitomo Bank Ltd, Sanwa Bank Ltd, Sakura Bank Ltd, Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi Ltd, Fuji Bank Ltd, Tokai Bank Ltd, Asahi Bank Ltd, Daiwa Bank Ltd, and Hokkaido Takushoku Bank Ltd.</p>
<p>BOT-Mitsubishi was formed in April 1996 from a merger between Mitsubishi Bank Ltd and Bank of Tokyo Ltd.</p>
</text>
